# Generated Python goldens (test/expected_*.py) are compared byte-for-byte
# against freshly emitted wrapper code, which JuliaLibWrapping always writes
# with LF line endings regardless of host OS. Force LF on checkout so a
# Windows `core.autocrlf` setting can't silently turn a golden into CRLF and
# break every golden-comparison test.
*.py text eol=lf
